# Developer / CI tooling.
#
# Separate from requirements.in so the production image does not need them.
# Install with the CI pins (= make install):
#   pip install -r requirements.lock -r requirements-dev.lock
#
# Regenerate the pinned dev lockfile (requirements-dev.lock) with:
#   make lock-dev
#
# The -c line keeps transitive deps shared with the runtime lock (requests,
# urllib3, packaging, ...) at the same pins, so
# `pip install -r requirements.lock -r requirements-dev.lock` never conflicts.
# Regenerate requirements.lock first.
-c requirements.lock

